{"title":"1964 AHSME Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/5/635bed6f608d7e48c515f090db8f196f1bee62c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=x^2+3x+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"150\" height=\"19\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/4/fa463f9f56b141367def53c8dd57070abfceb95d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{0, 1, 2, \\dots , 25 \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" />. \nThe number of members <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/e/4fe5a0767d0ef2863560208aafad9fcf14519053.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(s)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> has remainder zero when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/d/9dd91d1a075d793a50cb252ece243b69ce33d60e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 25\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 22\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 21\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 18 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/1/9914f8d2af05130dc2fb80653c22a99b50269ccc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = (x+1)(x+2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"173\" height=\"20\" />.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, then one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/cccb103143393c0119f5ab61d6d53a852ce70fcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8ab0ec5027c055e1b34dc345b1d8532b611bce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> is odd while the other is even.  So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is even for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then neither <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/cccb103143393c0119f5ab61d6d53a852ce70fcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> nor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8ab0ec5027c055e1b34dc345b1d8532b611bce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is not divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  \n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> has remainder <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8ab0ec5027c055e1b34dc345b1d8532b611bce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and so is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> has remainder <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/cccb103143393c0119f5ab61d6d53a852ce70fcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and so is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> which are not divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/b/bdb83422534bd215f170c73978e7cbfaac3534ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"64\" height=\"30\" /> such integers: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/a/86a00f070be7aa962dfb59d7326a4466fe61a54c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 4, 5, ..., 22, 23, 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"164\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that for all polynomials <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/f/caf1b0ce569c3c0eb5d44078cba61e3045bcdc0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x + 6) \\equiv f(x) \\pmod 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"197\" height=\"18\" />.  \n</p><p>Proof:\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/f/88f4842fb3a7e8fd0fd74c5287c1d872e1af3554.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = a_nx^n + a_{n-1}x^{n-1} + ... + a_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"267\" height=\"19\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/8/9b844114f8c17ec61fad42a9d88659b70304e03c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x+6) = a_n(x+6)^n + a_{n-1}(x+6)^{n-1} +...+ a_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"389\" height=\"19\" />.  In the second equation, we can use the binomial expansion to expand every term, and then subtract off all terms that have a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/3/353f68d49261d6db166aede2d54212312e0b17a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^1$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> or higher, since subtracting a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> will not change congruence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/f/caf79cc62b6d400782ab77bfe208d10c0bf4a480.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pmod 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />.  This leaves <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/e/f4e98f65bbac025f5c7d3360e38ef675f0772093.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_nx^n + a_{n-1}x^{n-1} + ... + a_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"207\" height=\"17\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/9/529fc6a6ba54d8d3d04afddf0e3651a185415a56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x+6) \\equiv f(x) \\pmod 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"197\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>So, we only need to test when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> has a remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/4/5c49e2cc4d2761ac7aedfa4540ebf241465a26c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" />.  The set of numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/d/acdb603232f0843540665625d986a92a0566cfd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"17\" /> will repeat remainders, as will all other sets.  The remainders are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/b/5eb006c1b7c8ca24078c56ef91eb6628b52a4231.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 0, 0, 2, 0, 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>This means for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/9/5d94b1601efd84048a7137a5407c7546c44e8ecd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=1, 2, 4, 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/e/4fe5a0767d0ef2863560208aafad9fcf14519053.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(s)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5b19bf7575fdc3655bb5767980f09dbb747a8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> is divisible, so is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/e/4fe5a0767d0ef2863560208aafad9fcf14519053.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(s)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/0/1e0756f1a9ffadfebb28ca6cefe31445a6395704.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=7, 13, 19, 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"120\" height=\"16\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> that work.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/2/562a91083e33775cdf050ea94f9e84d78a9c071c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> is divisible, so is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/e/4fe5a0767d0ef2863560208aafad9fcf14519053.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(s)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/7/7e74b5dfe3d1c5a40acd312b4c01a115d2e22553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=8, 14, 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> that work.  The values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302a64af3aa320ac53d2376ecc1c570594c741b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=4, 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" /> will also generate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> solutions each, just like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/2/562a91083e33775cdf050ea94f9e84d78a9c071c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />.  This is a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, for an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/f/6bfc0829f3f29bbf35d0a861644e00cfef0f50ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"39\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>We know that,</li></ul>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> +<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e634348f8df9eaeac4ced35db64d08a906532e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> congruent modulo 6 that implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/cccb103143393c0119f5ab61d6d53a852ce70fcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> or/and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8ab0ec5027c055e1b34dc345b1d8532b611bce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> congruent modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.The numbers are of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f74a2cb772128106ec44516d9daa604dced1fce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6k+5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/e/aded137b8305c9f57cbb519537e10dde79fe09a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6k+4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and due to restrictions of number of elements in the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> we get the inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/5/4d582dadf15143469157eefc67e782229437c7ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&lt;4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" />.Then we calculate the possible combinations to get  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> as answer i.e. option <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/f/6bfc0829f3f29bbf35d0a861644e00cfef0f50ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"39\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<pre>                                                                                                                                               <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e29ab247cd803dd1cee79ac4ae46e0d8bd135ff7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Solution$\" width=\"70\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/d/9ed8bd877353f4f9c1305efbcbebcea0ec506f74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$by$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/8/64841ed0a064a746d33d225ded612a6bcc3f2a0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GEOMETRY-WIZARD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"229\" height=\"16\" />\n</pre>\n<p>THE above solution does not give you the answer there are more cases,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e634348f8df9eaeac4ced35db64d08a906532e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> modulo 6 this has 4 cases,\nWhen, \n</p>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/cccb103143393c0119f5ab61d6d53a852ce70fcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> ≡ <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />(mod 6)</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8ab0ec5027c055e1b34dc345b1d8532b611bce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> ≡ <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />(mod 6)</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/cccb103143393c0119f5ab61d6d53a852ce70fcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> ≡ <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />(mod 6), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8ab0ec5027c055e1b34dc345b1d8532b611bce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> ≡ <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (mod 6)</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/cccb103143393c0119f5ab61d6d53a852ce70fcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> ≡ <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (mod 6), then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8ab0ec5027c055e1b34dc345b1d8532b611bce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> ≡ <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (mod 6), which satisfies.</li></ul>\n<p>Therefore by solvin' these cases we get 17.\n</p>\n<pre><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/f/b1f77807645649df9bfe61543a4d9e011069b94d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EDITED$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/d/9ed8bd877353f4f9c1305efbcbebcea0ec506f74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$by$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/b/ceb7e4207014d56edfb397f861d1dc9f7fe3e658.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RNVAA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />\n</pre>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/5/e85c86cb2b0b3d9787a3b6763813861739c37f5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(s)=s^2+3s+2=(s+1)(s+2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"279\" height=\"21\" />. The product of two consecutive numbers is always even i.e., divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. So, we are interested in finding all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/4/fa4f1f659ea5a289a0d8b827576e162351497439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s \\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/b/bab7af2e5ca83d8ec73dfa135ddb78a0fc175538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\mid (s+1)(s+2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"134\" height=\"20\" />. Since 3 is prime, we have that either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/f/b1fee3aa36f4774e32bdc25a14ee3906d61fb843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\mid s+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/f/47f889e8328c95f3c5f1a320b854fcf94c40d912.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\mid s+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"20\" />. For the first case, the number of multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/a/bda00d9a38a0c6bd9aac2512c6d065581882d43c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> inclusive is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and for each of them we can get a corresponding value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/4/fa4f1f659ea5a289a0d8b827576e162351497439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s \\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. Similarly, for the second case, the number of multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/1051e7d41ec0b8bd688a872be17538413f4ee97b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> inclusive is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and for each of them we can get a corresponding value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/4/fa4f1f659ea5a289a0d8b827576e162351497439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s \\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> as well. Thus, the total number of such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/1/2d148303486c77f7b6fb46f4ec73c0171d3d26f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8+9=\\boxed{(\\textbf{E}) \\, 17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"126\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>A (self) note for determining the intervals:\n</p><p>Case 1. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/9/af904c2ee5d9b8c1c392490e56828e2011e81a04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\quad 3 \\mid s+1 \\implies s+1 = 3k. \\; 0 \\le s \\le 25 \\implies 1 \\le 3k \\le 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"454\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Case 2. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/c/ddc9e810b60c1a6ce9bb6259ce90a98cb9e7aa4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\quad 3 \\mid s+2 \\implies s+2 = 3k. \\; 0 \\le s \\le 25 \\implies 2 \\le 3k \\le 27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"454\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>~ <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abbaa2d63b4b0621e038e82904fb55f2b59eadbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{N}\\text{oo}\\vec{\\text{r}}\\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><